   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Seam\n\nA transition between two panels: a colored silk-and-halftone material appears across the frame, the scene underneath swaps while it is opaque, then it dissolves in place to uncover the next. The block plays it between its own panels A and B, with text from variables; WebGL.\n\nCategory: shaders. Length: 5.2 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A shader material should dissolve in place to reveal the next scene.\n- A scene change needs an organic disappearance without directional travel.\n\nAvoid when:\n- A minimal typographic cut is enough: use caret-wipe.\n- The scenes themselves should be distorted at pixel level: use displacement.\n\nVariables:\n- softness (number, 0.02-0.4): Softness, default 0.18\n- detail (number, 0-1): Detail, default 0.65\n- speed (number, 0-3): Material speed, default 0\n- time_offset (number, 0-30): Material start time, default 0\n- a_label (string): Scene A label, default \"01 / Current scene\"\n- a_title (string): Scene A title, default \"Let it dissolve.\"\n- a_subtitle (string): Scene A line, default \"A moment between two scenes.\"\n- b_label (string): Scene B label, default \"02 / Next scene\"\n- b_title (string): Scene B title, default \"A new chapter.\"\n- b_subtitle (string): Scene B line, default \"Same frame. Another perspective.\"\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.5\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Shader Seam\n\n  Reveal a shader material, then dissolve it in place to uncover the next scene.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/shader-seam/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n\n  The field and halftone GLSL below are OpenShaders' original hero shaders (https://openshaders.com/@remocn),\n  shipped inside remocn's own source and licensed with it under the MIT licence above.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"shader-seam\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"5.2\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"softness\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Softness\", \"description\": \"Softness of the dissolve edge.\", \"default\": 0.18, \"min\": 0.02, \"max\": 0.4, \"step\": 0.01},\n    {\"id\": \"detail\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Detail\", \"description\": \"Organic variation mixed into the material's brightness.\", \"default\": 0.65, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.01},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Material speed\", \"description\": \"Animation speed of the material itself. 0 keeps it still.\", \"default\": 0, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 3, \"step\": 0.25},\n    {\"id\": \"time_offset\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Material start time\", \"description\": \"Starting time of the material, in seconds.\", \"default\": 0, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 30, \"step\": 0.5},\n    {\"id\": \"a_label\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Scene A label\", \"description\": \"Small label on the first scene.\", \"default\": \"01 / Current scene\"},\n    {\"id\": \"a_title\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Scene A title\", \"description\": \"Heading of the first scene.\", \"default\": \"Let it dissolve.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"a_subtitle\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Scene A line\", \"description\": \"Line under the first heading.\", \"default\": \"A moment between two scenes.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"b_label\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Scene B label\", \"description\": \"Small label on the second scene.\", \"default\": \"02 / Next scene\"},\n    {\"id\": \"b_title\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Scene B title\", \"description\": \"Heading of the second scene.\", \"default\": \"A new chapter.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"b_subtitle\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Scene B line\", \"description\": \"Line under the second heading.\", \"default\": \"Same frame. Another perspective.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the shader is drawn at, then scaled up. Lower renders faster; the material is drawn once at this size and held.\", \"default\": 0.5, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Shader Seam</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          background: var(--ssm-fallback, #14121c);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .ssm-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n        }\n        .ssm-scene { position: absolute; inset: 0; overflow: hidden; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; }\n        .ssm-a { background: #14121c; color: #f0ecf5; --ssm-line: #393040; }\n        .ssm-b { background: #e9e5ee; color: #25212d; --ssm-line: #b9afc8; visibility: hidden; }\n        .ssm-top { position: absolute; left: 5.6cqw; right: 5.6cqw; top: 5.6cqw; display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; font-size: 1.56cqw; opacity: 0.5; }\n        .ssm-copy { position: absolute; left: 5.6cqw; right: 5.6cqw; top: 19.6cqw; }\n        .ssm-title { font-size: 8.4cqw; letter-spacing: -0.47cqw; line-height: 1.05; font-weight: 600; }\n        .ssm-sub { font-size: 1.95cqw; margin-top: 2cqw; opacity: 0.5; }\n        .ssm-rings { position: absolute; right: -7.8cqw; bottom: -13.3cqw; width: 43.75cqw; height: 43.75cqw; border: 1px solid var(--ssm-line); border-radius: 50%; }\n        .ssm-rings div { position: absolute; inset: 4.5cqw; border: 1px solid var(--ssm-line); border-radius: 50%; }\n        .ssm-rings div + div { inset: 9cqw; }\n\n        .ssm-canvas {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: 100%;\n          display: block;\n        }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"shader-seam\" data-duration=\"5.2\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"ssm-clip\" class=\"ssm-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"5.2\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"ssm-scene-a\" class=\"ssm-scene ssm-a\">\n            <div class=\"ssm-top\"><span id=\"ssm-a-label\"></span></div>\n            <div class=\"ssm-copy\"><div class=\"ssm-title\" id=\"ssm-a-title\"></div><div class=\"ssm-sub\" id=\"ssm-a-sub\"></div></div>\n            <div class=\"ssm-rings\"><div></div><div></div></div>\n          </div>\n          <div id=\"ssm-scene-b\" class=\"ssm-scene ssm-b\">\n            <div class=\"ssm-top\"><span id=\"ssm-b-label\"></span></div>\n            <div class=\"ssm-copy\"><div class=\"ssm-title\" id=\"ssm-b-title\"></div><div class=\"ssm-sub\" id=\"ssm-b-sub\"></div></div>\n            <div class=\"ssm-rings\"><div></div><div></div></div>\n          </div>\n          <canvas id=\"ssm-canvas\" class=\"ssm-canvas\"></canvas>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"ssm-canvas\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, allowed, fallback) {\n              return allowed.indexOf(value) >= 0 ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function parseColor(s) {\n              var m = /^#?([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6}|[0-9a-f]{8})$/i.exec(String(s).trim());\n              if (!m) return null;\n              var h = m[1];\n              if (h.length === 3) h = h[0] + h[0] + h[1] + h[1] + h[2] + h[2];\n              var a = h.length === 8 ? parseInt(h.slice(6, 8), 16) / 255 : 1;\n              return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16) / 255, a];\n            }\n            function colorList(value, fallback, max) {\n              var list = String(typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback)\n                .split(\",\").map(parseColor).filter(Boolean).slice(0, max);\n              return list.length ? list : fallback.split(\",\").map(parseColor).slice(0, max);\n            }\n            function color(value, fallback) {\n              return parseColor(value) || parseColor(fallback);\n            }\n            function css(c) {\n              return \"rgba(\" + Math.round(c[0] * 255) + \",\" + Math.round(c[1] * 255) + \",\" + Math.round(c[2] * 255) + \",\" + c[3] + \")\";\n            }\n            function mulberry32(seed) {\n              return function () {\n                seed = (seed + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;\n                var t = Math.imul(seed ^ (seed >>> 15), 1 | seed);\n                t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\n                return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n              };\n            }\n            function colorArray(list, max) {\n              var flat = new Float32Array(max * 4);\n              list.forEach(function (c, i) { flat.set(c, i * 4); });\n              return flat;\n            }\n            var softness = num(vars.softness, 0.18, 0.02, 0.4);\n            var detail = num(vars.detail, 0.65, 0, 1);\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 0, 0, 3);\n            var timeOffset = num(vars.time_offset, 0, 0, 30);\n            var aLabel = typeof vars.a_label === \"string\" ? vars.a_label.slice(0, 200) : \"01 / Current scene\";\n            var aTitle = typeof vars.a_title === \"string\" ? vars.a_title.slice(0, 200) : \"Let it dissolve.\";\n            var aSubtitle = typeof vars.a_subtitle === \"string\" ? vars.a_subtitle.slice(0, 200) : \"A moment between two scenes.\";\n            var bLabel = typeof vars.b_label === \"string\" ? vars.b_label.slice(0, 200) : \"02 / Next scene\";\n            var bTitle = typeof vars.b_title === \"string\" ? vars.b_title.slice(0, 200) : \"A new chapter.\";\n            var bSubtitle = typeof vars.b_subtitle === \"string\" ? vars.b_subtitle.slice(0, 200) : \"Same frame. Another perspective.\";\n            var resolution = num(vars.resolution, 0.5, 0.25, 1);\n            var sceneA = document.getElementById(\"ssm-scene-a\");\n            var sceneB = document.getElementById(\"ssm-scene-b\");\n            document.getElementById(\"ssm-a-label\").textContent = aLabel;\n            document.getElementById(\"ssm-a-title\").textContent = aTitle;\n            document.getElementById(\"ssm-a-sub\").textContent = aSubtitle;\n            document.getElementById(\"ssm-b-label\").textContent = bLabel;\n            document.getElementById(\"ssm-b-title\").textContent = bTitle;\n            document.getElementById(\"ssm-b-sub\").textContent = bSubtitle;\n            // Without WebGL the block still shows its palette as a plain gradient.\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--ssm-fallback\", \"#14121c\");\n\n            function L(p, name) {\n              var m = p.__locs || (p.__locs = {});\n              if (!(name in m)) m[name] = gl.getUniformLocation(p, name);\n              return m[name];\n            }\n\n            var VERTEX = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  vec2 position = vec2(float((gl_VertexID << 1) & 2), float(gl_VertexID & 2));\",\n              \"  gl_Position = vec4(position * 2.0 - 1.0, 0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"}\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n\n            var FIELD = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"precision highp float;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"uniform vec2 iResolution;\",\n              \"uniform float iTime;\",\n              \"uniform float uLightMode;\",\n              \"uniform vec3 uDarkBackground;\",\n              \"uniform vec3 uLightBackground;\",\n              \"out vec4 fragColor;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"const float HUE = 0.663466752;\",\n              \"const float HUE_SPREAD = 0.314346701;\",\n              \"const float HUE_TRAVEL = 1.65112376;\",\n              \"const float CHROMA = 0.160295546;\",\n              \"const float LIGHTNESS = 0.537409723;\",\n              \"const float COLOUR_CYCLE = 0.124862425;\",\n              \"const float THETA = 2.12986207;\",\n              \"const float SHEAR = 0.968176901;\",\n              \"const float SHRINK = 0.955401778;\",\n              \"const float LAYERS = 72.0;\",\n              \"const float WARP_FREQ_X = 0.439311415;\",\n              \"const float WARP_FREQ_Y = 2.87923527;\",\n              \"const float WARP_AMP_X = 0.156202048;\",\n              \"const float WARP_AMP_Y = 0.0256033838;\",\n              \"const float ASPECT_X = 2.23183894;\",\n              \"const float ASPECT_Y = 0.15731883;\",\n              \"const float OFFSET_X = 0.375628948;\",\n              \"const float OFFSET_Y = -0.017801486;\",\n              \"const float TILT = 1.63293767;\",\n              \"const float ZOOM = 0.93135649;\",\n              \"const float CENTRE_X = -0.0956316143;\",\n              \"const float CENTRE_Y = -0.520057321;\",\n              \"const float GLOW_SIZE = 0.00201825937;\",\n              \"const float FALLOFF = 0.352821857;\",\n              \"const float VIGNETTE = 0.136085436;\",\n              \"const float FLOW_SPEED = 0.391012281;\",\n              \"const float FLOW_DIRECTION = 1.0;\",\n              \"const float BREATH_RATE = 0.382053256;\",\n              \"const float BREATH_AMOUNT = 0.0873704553;\",\n              \"const float PHASE = 56.3862724;\",\n              \"const float ECHO = 0.0;\",\n              \"const float ECHO_SHIFT = 0.178754866;\",\n              \"const float SOFTNESS = 0.00164903817;\",\n              \"const float LIGHT_SWING = 0.149726808;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"const float TAU = 6.28318530718;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"vec3 oklchToLinear(float L, float C, float h) {\",\n              \"  float a = C * cos(h), b = C * sin(h);\",\n              \"  float l_ = L + 0.3963377774 * a + 0.2158037573 * b;\",\n              \"  float m_ = L - 0.1055613458 * a - 0.0638541728 * b;\",\n              \"  float s_ = L - 0.0894841775 * a - 1.2914855480 * b;\",\n              \"  vec3 lms = vec3(l_, m_, s_);\",\n              \"  lms = lms * lms * lms;\",\n              \"  return mat3(4.0767416621, -1.2684380046, -0.0041960863,\",\n              \"              -3.3077115913, 2.6097574011, -0.7034186147,\",\n              \"              0.2309699292, -0.3413193965, 1.7076147010) * lms;\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"\",\n              \"float blueNoise(vec2 p, float frame) {\",\n              \"  p += 5.588238 * mod(frame, 64.0);\",\n              \"  return fract(52.9829189 * fract(0.06711056 * p.x + 0.00583715 * p.y));\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  vec2 R = iResolution.xy;\",\n              \"  vec2 pos = (gl_FragCoord.xy - 0.5 * R) / R.y;\",\n              \"  float t = iTime * FLOW_SPEED * FLOW_DIRECTION + PHASE;\",\n              \"  float breath = (-sin(iTime * BREATH_RATE * 1.5) + sin(iTime * BREATH_RATE + 1.0)) * 0.25 + 0.5;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  vec2 u = (pos - vec2(CENTRE_X, CENTRE_Y)) * (ZOOM - breath * BREATH_AMOUNT);\",\n              \"  float ct = cos(TILT), st = sin(TILT);\",\n              \"  u = mat2(ct, st, -st, ct) * u;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  mat2 fold = mat2(cos(THETA), sin(THETA), -SHEAR, cos(THETA));\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  float hue0 = HUE * TAU;\",\n              \"  float hue1 = hue0 + HUE_SPREAD * TAU;\",\n              \"  vec3 color = vec3(0.0);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  for (float i = 1.0; i <= 96.0; i += 1.0) {\",\n              \"    if (i > LAYERS) break;\",\n              \"    u.x += -sin(u.y * WARP_FREQ_X + t + i * 0.007) * WARP_AMP_X;\",\n              \"    u.y += -sin(u.x * WARP_FREQ_Y - t + i * 0.02) * WARP_AMP_Y;\",\n              \"    u = fold * u * SHRINK;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"    vec2 q = u - vec2(OFFSET_X + breath * 0.1, OFFSET_Y);\",\n              \"    vec2 s = vec2(q.x * ASPECT_X, q.y * ASPECT_Y);\",\n              \"    float glow = GLOW_SIZE / (dot(s, s) + SOFTNESS);\",\n              \"#ifndef SKIP_ECHO\",\n              \"    vec2 e = vec2((q.x - ECHO_SHIFT) * ASPECT_X, s.y);\",\n              \"    glow += ECHO * GLOW_SIZE / (dot(e, e) + SOFTNESS);\",\n              \"#endif\",\n              \"    glow *= 0.25 + breath * 0.4;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"    float r = length(u);\",\n              \"    float k = sin(i * COLOUR_CYCLE + t * 1.2 + r * HUE_TRAVEL) * 0.5 + 0.5;\",\n              \"    vec3 tint = clamp(oklchToLinear(LIGHTNESS + LIGHT_SWING * k, CHROMA * (0.75 + 0.35 * k), mix(hue0, hue1, k)), 0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"    color += glow * tint * exp2(-r * FALLOFF);\",\n              \"  }\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  vec3 x = max(color, 0.0);\",\n              \"  color = (x * (2.51 * x + 0.03)) / (x * (2.43 * x + 0.59) + 0.14);\",\n              \"  color = pow(clamp(color, 0.0, 1.0), vec3(0.85, 0.92, 0.98));\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  float edge = smoothstep(0.5, 1.6, length(pos));\",\n              \"  color *= 1.0 - edge * VIGNETTE;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  vec3 dark = uDarkBackground + color * (1.0 - uDarkBackground);\",\n              \"  float strength = max(color.r, max(color.g, color.b));\",\n              \"  vec3 light = uLightBackground * (1.0 - strength) + color * 0.96;\",\n              \"  color = mix(dark, light, uLightMode);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"  color += (blueNoise(gl_FragCoord.xy, floor(iTime * 24.0)) - 0.5) / 255.0;\",\n              \"  fragColor = vec4(clamp(color, 0.0, 1.0), 1.0);\",\n              \"}\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n\n            var RARITY = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"precision highp float;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"uniform sampler2D tScene;\",\n              \"uniform vec2 iResolution;\",\n              \"uniform float iTime;\",\n              \"uniform float uLightMode;\",\n              \"uniform vec3 uDarkBackground;\",\n              \"uniform vec3 uLightBackground;\",\n              \"uniform float uPixelRatio;\",\n              \"out vec4 fragColor;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"const float uStrength = 0.797335207;\",\n              \"const float uScale = 0.985214949;\",\n              \"const float uSeed = 0.435611069;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"const float TAU = 6.28318530718;\",\n              \"const vec3 LUMA = vec3(0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722);\",\n              \"\",\n              \"vec3 toInk(vec3 c) { return mix(c - uDarkBackground, uLightBackground - c, uLightMode); }\",\n              \"vec3 fromInk(vec3 ink) { return mix(uDarkBackground + ink, uLightBackground - ink, uLightMode); }\",\n              \"vec3 sceneInk(vec2 uv) { return toInk(texture(tScene, clamp(uv, 0.0, 1.0)).rgb); }\",\n              \"\",\n              \"float blueNoise(vec2 p, float frame) {\",\n              \"  p += 5.588238 * mod(frame, 64.0);\",\n              \"  return fract(52.9829189 * fract(0.06711056 * p.x + 0.00583715 * p.y));\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"\",\n              \"vec3 halftone(vec2 frag) {\",\n              \"  float cell = max(3.0, uScale * 3.6 * uPixelRatio);\",\n              \"  float angle = 0.26 + uSeed * 0.3;\",\n              \"  mat2 turn = mat2(cos(angle), -sin(angle), sin(angle), cos(angle));\",\n              \"  vec2 rotated = turn * frag;\",\n              \"  vec2 grid = floor(rotated / cell);\",\n              \"  vec2 centre = (grid + 0.5) * cell;\",\n              \"  vec2 source = transpose(turn) * centre;\",\n              \"  vec3 soft = sceneInk(frag / iResolution);\",\n              \"  vec3 ink = sceneInk(source / iResolution);\",\n              \"  float level = clamp(dot(ink, LUMA), 0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"  float radius = cell * sqrt(pow(level, 0.9) / 3.14159265);\",\n              \"  float dist = length(rotated - centre);\",\n              \"  float aa = 0.7 * uPixelRatio;\",\n              \"  float dot_ = 1.0 - smoothstep(radius - aa, radius + aa, dist);\",\n              \"  vec3 dots = ink * min(0.8 / max(level, 1e-3), 2.2) * dot_;\",\n              \"  float presence = smoothstep(0.03, 0.16, level) * (0.3 + 0.14 * uStrength);\",\n              \"  return mix(soft, dots, presence);\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  vec2 frag = gl_FragCoord.xy;\",\n              \"  vec3 ink = halftone(frag);\",\n              \"  vec3 color = fromInk(clamp(ink, 0.0, 1.0));\",\n              \"  color += (blueNoise(frag, floor(iTime * 24.0)) - 0.5) / 255.0;\",\n              \"  fragColor = vec4(clamp(color, 0.0, 1.0), 1.0);\",\n              \"}\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n\n            var DISSOLVE = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"precision highp float;\",\n              \"uniform vec2 iResolution;\",\n              \"uniform sampler2D tScene;\",\n              \"uniform sampler2D tField;\",\n              \"uniform float uPresence;\",\n              \"uniform float uDissolve;\",\n              \"uniform float uSoftness;\",\n              \"uniform float uDetail;\",\n              \"out vec4 fragColor;\",\n              \"\",\n              \"float hash(vec2 p) {\",\n              \"  return fract(sin(dot(p, vec2(127.1, 311.7))) * 43758.5453);\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"float noise(vec2 p) {\",\n              \"  vec2 i = floor(p), f = fract(p);\",\n              \"  f = f * f * (3.0 - 2.0 * f);\",\n              \"  return mix(mix(hash(i), hash(i + vec2(1, 0)), f.x),\",\n              \"    mix(hash(i + vec2(0, 1)), hash(i + vec2(1, 1)), f.x), f.y);\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  vec2 uv = gl_FragCoord.xy / iResolution;\",\n              \"  vec2 p = gl_FragCoord.xy / iResolution.y;\",\n              \"  vec3 field = texture(tField, uv).rgb;\",\n              \"  float energy = max(field.r, max(field.g, field.b));\",\n              \"  // Static, continuous noise breaks up the field without making it travel.\",\n              \"  float grain = noise(p * 7.0) * 0.6 + noise(p * 19.0) * 0.28\",\n              \"    + noise(p * 43.0) * 0.12;\",\n              \"  float density = mix(smoothstep(0.025, 0.95, energy), grain, uDetail * 0.55);\",\n              \"  float appear = mix(1.0 + uSoftness, -uSoftness, uPresence);\",\n              \"  float disappear = mix(-uSoftness, 1.0 + uSoftness, uDissolve);\",\n              \"  float alpha = smoothstep(appear - uSoftness, appear + uSoftness, density)\",\n              \"    * smoothstep(disappear - uSoftness, disappear + uSoftness, density);\",\n              \"  vec3 material = texture(tScene, uv).rgb;\",\n              \"  fragColor = vec4(material * alpha, alpha);\",\n              \"}\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n\n            // The canvas is drawn at `resolution` × the frame size and stretched to fill it.\n            var width = Math.max(2, Math.round(root.clientWidth * resolution));\n            var height = Math.max(2, Math.round(root.clientHeight * resolution));\n            canvas.width = width;\n            canvas.height = height;\n            var gl = canvas.getContext(\"webgl2\", { alpha: true, premultipliedAlpha: true, antialias: false, depth: false, stencil: false, preserveDrawingBuffer: true });\n\n            function compile(type, source) {\n              var s = gl.cre